    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0958" n="830" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg830"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.796/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-03T17:00:00-04:30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1928—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:16 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>71. My telegram No. 70, July 3, 4 p.m. I have been given to understand that the
                    United States has been rather slow in entering this field,<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d684-f1"/> and that it cannot hope to keep out foreign interests
                    indefinitely.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
